From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:33:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/79] lanes: runner rounds: drafts past a forced tail,
 settled fires, the round trace

The rounds side of the in-model runner (slice 6 of C4).

- forced_drafts.zig: a lone window holding a forced tail (a runner's or a
  tool's result) takes the last fed row's drafts past it. Config.forced_drafts
  is off for every family by default; DeepSeek-V4.1's lane model turns it on as
  before (TF_DSV41_NO_FORCED_DRAFTS=1 turns it off). forced_drafts.headDepth
  sizes the head's drafts past the tail (the unforced depth plus the tail, at
  most the stream's room); backend.Window.forced names the forced rows for a
  backend.
- A settled trigger's last kept token reruns as a held EOS does (settle .cut),
  so a fire settled at its trigger never holds: settle_fire_test and
  test-settle-fire-host.
- round_trace.zig: rounds around each held stream, one JSON line each,
  read-only (off on Windows at compile time). runner_binding.openRoundTrace
  opens it from PREFIX_TRACE (1: stderr, else a path) and PREFIX_TRACE_ROUNDS;
  DeepSeek-V4.1's serve engine calls it beside the runner. The fork's DSV41
  backend counters (row graphs, DSpark spec, Engram) are not in this trace.
- fire_replay_test and round_trace_test.

Ported from the dsv41 release line (s86 7b79ef92d).
